-- gate: reject
-- defect: a bare constructor an import binds over the Prelude's of the same name
-- rust: reject [E1017] constructor clash, reported at the use site
--
-- Found 2026-10-26. `Sky.Config.LogLevel` has a constructor `Error`, the name
-- of the Prelude's `Error` too. After `exposing (LogLevel(..))`, the bare
-- `Error` below, written for the Prelude's `Error`, silently meant
-- `LogLevel.Error`, and the user got `type mismatch: LogLevel vs ErrorKind ->
-- _` with no word about the import. Now the reference is `[E1017]`, which names
-- both meanings and the qualified forms (`Config.Error`, `E.Error`).
--
-- The ACCEPTED twins (the qualified forms, an import whose `Error` is never
-- written bare, a local constructor) are in `hir/tests/ctor_clash.rs`.
module Main exposing (main)

import Sky.Core.Prelude exposing (..)
import Sky.Core.Error as E
import Sky.Config as Config exposing (LogLevel(..))


failure : E.Error
failure =
    Error E.Io { message = "disk full", details = Nothing }


main =
    failure
